@page "/contact"

<PageTitle>Contact &amp; Support — QuickResult</PageTitle>

<article class="doc-page contact-page">
    <h1>Contact &amp; Support</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Found a bug, missing an overload, or unsure which combinator fits? Two good routes:
    </p>

    <div class="contact-cards">
        <div class="contact-card">
            <h2>Email support</h2>
            <p>
                For questions, feedback, or anything you'd rather not post publicly:
            </p>
            <p class="contact-address">
                <a href="mailto:support@quickresult.net">support@quickresult.net</a>
            </p>
            <p class="contact-note">
                Read by a human — replies typically within a few days.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="contact-card">
            <h2>GitHub issues</h2>
            <p>
                Bugs and feature requests are best filed where they can be tracked (and where others
                can find the answer later):
            </p>
            <p class="contact-address">
                <a href="https://github.com/aaroncpina/QuickResult/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    github.com/aaroncpina/QuickResult/issues
                </a>
            </p>
            <p class="contact-note">
                Please include your QuickResult and .NET versions, and a minimal snippet that reproduces
                the behavior.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Everything else</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Package: <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/QuickResult/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nuget.org/packages/QuickResult</a></li>
        <li>Source &amp; README: <a href="https://github.com/aaroncpina/QuickResult" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/aaroncpina/QuickResult</a></li>
        <li>License: MIT — free for commercial use.</li>
    </ul>
</article>
